# Curated, moderate check set: real-bug-finding groups (bugprone, the static
# analyzer, performance, portability) plus a hand-picked list of readability
# and modernize checks. Full readability-*/modernize-*/cppcoreguidelines-*
# groups were deliberately left out — they mostly flag this project's
# existing style (no trailing return types, short loop/parameter names,
# member init style) rather than real issues.
#
# readability-redundant-declaration is intentionally not enabled: it false
# positives on the implicit global module fragment's redeclaration of
# ::operator new/delete for every C++20 module interface unit here.
#
# bugprone-reserved-identifier is intentionally excluded: clang-tidy-20
# reliably segfaults running it (RenamerClangTidyCheck) against
# src/modules/ast.cppm, which would otherwise abort analysis of that file
# entirely.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-reserved-identifier,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  modernize-use-nullptr,
  modernize-use-override,
  modernize-use-emplace,
  modernize-use-default-member-init,
  modernize-use-equals-default,
  modernize-use-equals-delete,
  modernize-loop-convert,
  modernize-redundant-void-arg,
  modernize-use-bool-literals,
  modernize-use-using,
  modernize-make-unique,
  modernize-make-shared,
  readability-braces-around-statements,
  readability-container-size-empty,
  readability-delete-null-pointer,
  readability-else-after-return,
  readability-inconsistent-declaration-parameter-name,
  readability-misleading-indentation,
  readability-non-const-parameter,
  readability-redundant-control-flow,
  readability-redundant-member-init,
  readability-redundant-string-cstr,
  readability-redundant-string-init,
  readability-simplify-boolean-expr,
  readability-static-accessed-through-instance,
  readability-uniqueptr-delete-release

WarningsAsErrors: ''
FormatStyle: file